// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`C10 §4k — the compositions, as frames > case 1 — focused + selected + failed, at 1-bit 1`] = `
"-- the frame
    Name          State     
    alpha         ✓ running 
  ▸ bravo         ✗ failed                
    charlie       ✓ running 

-- which fact took the ground, run by run
  dim/-:"Name        " dim/-:"State     "
  page/-:"  alpha         " bold/-:"✓ running "
  inverse+bold/-:"▸ " inverse/-:"bravo         " inverse+bold/-:"✗ failed  "
  page/-:"  charlie       " bold/-:"✓ running "

-- without copy selection, run by run
  dim/-:"Name        " dim/-:"State     "
  page/-:"  alpha         " bold/-:"✓ running "
  bold/-:"▸ " page/-:"bravo         " bold/-:"✗ failed  "
  page/-:"  charlie       " bold/-:"✓ running "

-- without focus, run by run
  dim/-:"Name        " dim/-:"State     "
  page/-:"  alpha         " bold/-:"✓ running "
  inverse/-:"  bravo         " inverse+bold/-:"✗ failed  "
  page/-:"  charlie       " bold/-:"✓ running "

-- without failure, run by run
  dim/-:"Name        " dim/-:"State     "
  page/-:"  alpha         " bold/-:"✓ running "
  inverse+bold/-:"▸ " inverse/-:"bravo         " inverse+bold/-:"✓ running "
  page/-:"  charlie       " bold/-:"✓ running "

-- the ruling (C10 §4k.2 row 1)
  selection takes the ground · focus keeps its mark · failure keeps its glyph, its word and its tone

-- and what drawing it found, kept because the record is the point
  This frame reported two of row 1's three clauses for as long as it existed. A focused or
  selected row was repainted in ONE ink — accent, or default under selection — so \`failed\` kept
  ✗ and the word and lost the error tone. The two halves of the remedy were one change and
  neither worked alone: C11 I14's drop-to-one-ink rule, and a painter that resolves a tone
  against the surface it lands on. \`inkOn\` was that resolver and was called only from
  \`contrast.ts\` — 74 of 100 tone x surface pairs were an ink the gate checked and the painter
  never emitted. C10 I48 gives \`resolve\` the ground, \`inkOn\` is its composition step, and the
  ink beside each ground above is the value C10 T2.49 measures the gate against."
`;

